Appendix B. Modal Decoupling and the Energetic Metric

Setup. Write L_G=U\Lambda U^\top with U orthogonal and \Lambda=\operatorname{diag}(0,\lambda_2,\dots,\lambda_N), 0<\lambda_2\le\cdots\le\lambda_N. The first column of U is \phi_1=N^{-1/2}\mathbf 1.

Proposition B.1 (modal decoupling). Let c(t)=U^\top x(t) and \tilde v(t)=U^\top v(t). Then the controlled dynamics \dot x=-L_Gx+v is equivalent to

\dot c_1=0,\qquad \dot c_k=-\lambda_k c_k+\tilde v_k,\quad k=2,\dots,N.

Proof. Multiply \dot x=-L_Gx+v on the left by U^\top:

U^\top\dot x=-U^\top L_Gx+U^\top v=-U^\top L_GU\,U^\top x+\tilde v=-\Lambda c+\tilde v.

Componentwise, \dot c_1=-\lambda_1c_1+\tilde v_1. Because L_G\mathbf 1=0, \lambda_1=0, and because v\in\mathbf 1^\perp, \tilde v_1=\phi_1^\top v=N^{-1/2}\mathbf 1^\top v=0. Hence \dot c_1=0, i.e., c_1(t)=c_1(0)=N^{-1/2}I(x). \square

Proposition B.2 (energetic metric). For v\in\mathbf 1^\perp,

v^\top L_G^+v=\sum_{k=2}^N\frac{\tilde v_k^2}{\lambda_k}.

Proof. Since L_G^+=U\Lambda^+U^\top with \Lambda^+=\operatorname{diag}(0,\lambda_2^{-1},\dots,\lambda_N^{-1}),

v^\top L_G^+v=(U^\top v)^\top\Lambda^+(U^\top v)=\sum_{k=2}^N\frac{\tilde v_k^2}{\lambda_k}.\qquad\square

