Appendix H. Spectral Bounds

Proposition H.1. On \mathbf 1^\perp,

\frac{1}{\lambda_N}I_\perp\preceq L_G^+\preceq\frac{1}{\lambda_2}I_\perp,

and consequently, for every v\in\mathbf 1^\perp,

\frac{\|v\|_2^2}{\lambda_N}\le v^\top L_G^+v\le\frac{\|v\|_2^2}{\lambda_2}.

Proof. Let v=\sum_{k\ge2}\alpha_k\phi_k, where \{\phi_k\}_{k\ge2} is the orthonormal eigenbasis of L_G on \mathbf 1^\perp. Then

v^\top L_G^+v=\sum_{k\ge2}\frac{\alpha_k^2}{\lambda_k}.

Since \lambda_2\le\lambda_k\le\lambda_N for every k\ge2, we have

\frac{\alpha_k^2}{\lambda_N}\le\frac{\alpha_k^2}{\lambda_k}\le\frac{\alpha_k^2}{\lambda_2}.

Summing over k and using \|v\|_2^2=\sum_{k\ge2}\alpha_k^2 gives the result. The operator inequalities follow from the spectral representation L_G^+=\sum_{k\ge2}\lambda_k^{-1}\phi_k\phi_k^\top on \mathbf 1^\perp. \square

