Appendix I. Invariance of the Mean under Active Control

Proposition I.1. Under \dot x=-L_Gx+v with v\in\mathbf 1^\perp, I(x(t))=I(x(0)) for all t.

Proof.

\frac{d}{dt}I(x(t))=\mathbf 1^\top\dot x=-\mathbf 1^\top L_Gx+\mathbf 1^\top v.

Because L_G is symmetric and L_G\mathbf 1=0, we have \mathbf 1^\top L_G=(L_G\mathbf 1)^\top=0, so \mathbf 1^\top L_Gx=0. Also \mathbf 1^\top v=0 by hypothesis. Hence dI/dt=0. \square

Corollary I.2. If v=Bu for some u\in\mathbb R^M, then v\in\operatorname{Range}(B)=\mathbf 1^\perp, so I is automatically conserved.

Proof. \mathbf 1^\top B=0 because each column of B has one +1 and one -1. Hence \mathbf 1^\top Bu=0. \square

