Appendix K. Thermodynamic Qualification

Proposition K.1. The functional \int_0^\tau v^\top L_G^+v\,dt equals the minimum active edge-current dissipation \int_0^\tau u_{\rm active}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm active}\,dt over active currents u_{\rm active} with Bu_{\rm active}=v, and is not equal in general to the total network edge dissipation \int_0^\tau u_{\rm tot}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm tot}\,dt, where u_{\rm tot}=u_{\rm active}+u_{\rm passive} and u_{\rm passive} generates the passive term -L_Gx.

Proof. By Theorem 1 applied pointwise in time, the minimum active dissipation realizing v(t) is v(t)^\top L_G^+v(t). For the total dissipation, the passive dynamics -L_Gx itself corresponds to an edge current u_{\rm passive} with Bu_{\rm passive}=-L_Gx; explicitly, since -L_Gx\in\mathbf 1^\perp=\operatorname{Range}(B), there exists a unique minimum-norm u_{\rm passive} with Bu_{\rm passive}=-L_Gx. The total edge current is u_{\rm tot}=u_{\rm active}+u_{\rm passive}, and

u_{\rm tot}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm tot}
=u_{\rm active}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm active}+u_{\rm passive}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm passive}+2u_{\rm active}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm passive}.

The cross term is generally nonzero. Hence total dissipation \ne active dissipation. \square

Corollary K.2. Under the constitutive identification J_e=L_eF_e with L_e=G_e, the entropy production rate T\dot S_i=J_e^\top L_e^{-1}J_e evaluates to u_{\rm tot}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm tot} when the total edge current is u_{\rm tot}. The quantity v^\top L_G^+v=u_{\rm active}^\top G_e^{-1}u_{\rm active} is the active contribution only.

Proof. Immediate from the constitutive law and the definition of u_{\rm tot}.

