D1. Zhang, Y., Ouyang, Q., & Tu, Y. (2025). Geometry of optimal control in chemical reaction networks in the adiabatic limit. Physical Review Letters, 134, 018001. 
Annotation. Derives a “Kirchhoff’s law” for probability currents in the adiabatic limit, shows that minimum-dissipation protocols are geodesics in probability space, and gives an analytical expression for the metric tensor depending on network topology and link capacities. Directly supports the edge-space dissipation functional u^\top G_e^{-1}u and its thermodynamic interpretation in Section 6 and Section 13.

